I've now had five excellent games of 3.0.9 and 3.0.10, games in which I
reached the castle.  In one, I carelessly stepped into the moat.  In
another, the game was set up wrong, allowing me to be killed by trickery
after a save/restore.  And the other three were all terminated by the
same monster, the invulnerable Segmentation Fault.

Is it possible to set up the code so that it at least attempts to do a
panic save after a seg fault?  When older versions of Moria seg-faulted
and panic saved, the game could often be recovered by discarding the
offending item and going to another level.  If Nethack at least tried to
recreate the level on a seg fault (with the usual "the dungeon
collapses"), it might be possible to recover the game.

